# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Use KEY=value with no spaces around `=`.
#
# During /setup, Claude extends this file with the project's real variables
# (API URLs, publishable keys, service DSNs, …) and comments on where each
# value comes from.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Task Master AI (CLI/MCP) — ALL OPTIONAL with this template.
# .taskmaster/config.json uses the `claude-code` provider, which reuses your
# Claude Code session — no API key needed. Only add keys here if you switch to
# API-based models or want `--research` mode (Perplexity recommended for that).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-api03-..."
#PERPLEXITY_API_KEY="pplx-..."
#OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-..."
#GOOGLE_API_KEY="..."
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY="..."

# ── Project variables (added during /setup)
#
# NOTE (Cloudflare Workers): the Worker runtime does NOT read .env. Local dev
# secrets go in `.dev.vars` (gitignored, same KEY=value format); production
# secrets are set with `wrangler secret put <KEY>`. The variables below are
# documented here as the canonical list — copy the ones you need to .dev.vars.

# Stripe (test mode until launch) — from https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
#STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="sk_test_..."
# Webhook signing secret — from the Stripe webhook endpoint config (or
# `stripe listen --print-secret` for local testing)
#STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_..."

# x402 agent payments (OPTIONAL — feature stays dark until set)
# USDC receiving wallet address on Base
#X402_WALLET_ADDRESS="0x..."

# Admin token for manual ops endpoints (generate: `openssl rand -hex 32`)
#ADMIN_TOKEN=""

# CI deploys (GitHub Actions secret, not used locally):
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN — create at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
# with the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template.
